(ARG-48 — *(not a manual claim — a gap in the manual)* a number flag
 given a decimal value truncates toward zero, silently: no error flag,
 no diagnostic, 1.5 becomes 1. Unlike ARG-46 and ARG-47 there is nothing
 for a program to notice.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox ARG-48.vox -o p && ./p -r 1.5
 Args: -r 1.5
 expected output:
   retries is 1
)
a flag called retries is "-r" or "--retries", it is a number.
Parse flags.

a number called seen is retries.
